  "date": "2026-08-18",
  "purpose": "Build and validate the minimal runtime KV relocate/rebind primitive Phase 12C identified as missing: an actual llama.cpp method that reassigns a live llama_kv_cache layer's backing tensor after a real byte copy, so the NEXT decode call reads the relocated data (true runtime relocation, not just a copy).",
  "literal_verdict": "RUNTIME_KV_RELOCATE_WORKS_BUT_LEAKS_BACKING",
  "verdict_summary": "A small (173 insertion lines, 0 deletions, 4 files), additive llama.cpp patch adding llama_kv_cache::relocate_layer() makes runtime rebind real: ground-truth poison testing (not just code reading) proves decode consumes the newly-rebound backing, in both directions (CPU->GPU, GPU->CPU), repeatedly, for the same layer, across two models and two KV precisions. But the old backing cannot yet be safely freed: with the real default (release enabled), a SECOND relocation of the same layer reproducibly crashes the NEXT llama_decode() call (two observed signatures: SIGSEGV and GGML_ASSERT(buffer != nullptr) at ggml-vulkan.cpp:7815). This is disclosed as a genuine, unresolved negative finding, not softened -- old backing must be retained (leaked) to remain safe this phase.",
  "verdict_source": "results/phase12/runtime-relocate/summary.json:decision_gate / decision_gate_meaning (literal source fields, not synthesized)",
  "productized": false,
  "product_pr": null,
  "product_commit": null,
  "productization_note": "Verified: `git grep` for relocate_layer / llama_kv_cache_relocate_layer against product main returns no hits. This mechanism, including its known crash, remains entirely research-only -- it was never a candidate for productization in its own right; it motivated Phase 12E's fix instead.",
  "reproducibility": "PARTIALLY_REPRODUCIBLE",
  "hardware": "NVIDIA GTX 1650 (4096 MiB VRAM), Vulkan backend",
